    <values><field>LongDescription__c</field><value xsi:type="xsd:string">Finds: SBQQ__Subscription__c records where SBQQ__Quantity__c &gt; 1000.
Why it matters: Unusually high quantities can be legitimate (seat-based enterprise licensing) or a data-entry error (extra zero on the quantity). Worth surfacing for review on every detection.
Suppress a finding: when the high quantity matches the customer contract (note the contract number).
Disable the detector: only if four-digit quantities are common. Most should leave this on.</value></values>
